      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk, it feels like you're saying highway expansion is just a problem to be solved rather than a real way to help people. if we just keep pushing transit as the \"sustainable solution,\" aren't we basically just telling people in certain parts of the state that their way of life/needs are obsolete or just \"wrong\" for the environment? how can you say highway expansion isn't a legitimate, essential part of growth?",
